  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Central Darfur - North Jabal Marra 2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtltbrgtThe project aims to reduce childhood morbidity and mortality by addressing the identified gaps and enabling access to integrated multisectoral life-saving services that include the provision of primary health and malnutrition treatment and preventive care, safe water and sanitation, and protection services aligning with the HRP&apos;s strategic objective (SO1) that aims to provide life-saving humanitarian assistance, targeting the most vulnerable groups to reduce mortality and morbidity. The health and nutrition activities will aim to provide the needed Primary Health Care (PHC) and nutritional assistance for beneficiaries in North Jebal Marra and Azum locality. The proposed WASH activities aim to enhance access to safe water, sanitation, and hygiene knowledge for approximately 20,000 beneficiaries, prioritizing the rehabilitation of four water yards with solar systems, serving an average of 5,000 individuals (5,304 girls, 5,096 boys, 4,896 women, and 4,704 men). Integrated efforts include linking water sources to health facilities and the catchment population. Solid waste management initiatives target 2,400 individuals through cleaning campaigns and waste disposal, ensuring a safe environment. Additionally, 150 people benefit from new latrine blocks at health facilities, reducing disease risks. Save the Children&apos;s comprehensive approach, encompassing environmental and social considerations, promotes sustainability and resilience in Azum and Shamal Jebel Marra, aligning with climate-resilient practices and environmental conservation . Also, this project will be providing and improving protection services to 875 beneficiaries in Zalinge locality. Those services will be provided by HOPE a partner to SCI who will coordinate the protection services along with other SCI interventions within the same locality to ensure integration. Another partner, SORR will be supporting the distribution of seeds to selected beneficiaries in both Zalinge and Azum localities, supported by SCI Cash distribution to ensure that the basic needs of the beneficiaries are met.lt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
